  "family": "Rosaceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Prunus serrulata &lt;/em&gt;is a popular, modestly-sized flowering tree native to south and east China, Japan, and Korea. Its delicate leaves have toothed margins, referred to by its epithet, &lt;em&gt;serrulata&lt;/em&gt;. Its pink to white blooms are exceptionally ornamental, blanketing the entire leafless canopy in spring. While the species itself is uncommon in cultivation, it has given rise to numerous cultivars and varieties that differ in canopy shape and bloom color. Aditionally, fall foliage varies from shades of yellow to bronze. This tree flowers best in full sun and requires good drainage to succeed.&nbsp;",
